```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
Due to the Presidents Day holiday, a meeting of the Public Services Committee was instead held
on Tuesday, February 18, 2025, in Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting. starring at
12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Tom Segrave, Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Mark Moody; and
Jeff 1hite. Absent: Dr. Kathy Emmons.
AGENDA ITEMS
7.
ORDINANCE --3’ READING
— Amending various sections of Chapter 15.08, 15.09,
15.10, 15.12, 15.16, 15.22, 15.24 and 15.26 ofTitle 15, Buildings and Construction, ofthe
Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, updating specified Building Code
requirements and making technical corrections as further specified.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3r’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. White. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Antony Pomerleau, Chief Building Official, provided a staff report and advised there have been
no changes or comments since approval on 2 reading. Committee member Aldrich commented
on the item.
8.
ORDINANCE —3” READING
— Amending various sections within Chapter 8.12,
International Fire Code adopted, of Title 8, Health and Safety, of the Municipal Code of
the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming. updating the edition of the International Fire Code
adopted by the City and further amending as specified.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. White. Dr. Aldrich moved
to amend by substitute dated February 13,2025, seconded by Mr. White. Motion to amend carried
by unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as amended, carried by unanimous voice vote.
Bob Mason, Fire Marshal, Fire Rescue Department, provided a staff report and a proposed
substitute. Committee members Aldrich and White commented on the item.
9.
ORDINANCE -3 READING
— Amending section 8.24.020 of the Municipal Code of the
City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, clarifying and further regulating the installation of above-
ground tanks and containers as specified.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Bob Mason. Fire Marshal. Fire Rescue Department, provided a staffreport and committee member
Aldrich commented on the item.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
10.
ORDINANCE _2l READING
— Repealing the provisions for the Paid On-Street Parking
Districts program of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, further
amending the regulatory authority governing parking in Cheyenne and abrogating any On-
Street Parking District designated by Resolution of the Governing Body. (Sponsors
— Dr.
Aldrich, Mr. Layboum, Mr. Moody and Mr. White)
Dr Aldrich moved to approve on
reading, seconded by Mr. Whtie.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Dr. Aldrich, sponsor of the item, provided an overview of the proposed ordinance noting the
downtown property owner’s strong opposition to the recently approved paid parking program. Dr.
Aldrich thanked thc Cheyenne Police Department for time and effort put forth to the recently
approved parking program. Committee member Moody commented on the item as did committee
member White who also thanked staff for their time and effort Public comments in support of
repealing the ordinance were made by Susan Allen, Rob Dickerson, Sam Galeotos and Glen
Garrett.
11.
ORDINANCE 201 READING
— Amending Sections 1.4.4,5.1.4 and 5.7.10, of the Unified
Development Code to remove the land use term ‘Work Camps’ and prohibit their
establishment within the City. (Sponsors
— Dr. Aldrich, Mr. Moody, Dr. Rinne, Mr.
Segrave and Mr. White)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on
2nd reading, seconded by Mr. White.
Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Charles Bloom, Planning
& Development Department Director, provided
a staff report.
Committee members Aldrich and Moody commented on the item.
12.
RESOLUTION
- Approving the ‘2024 Cheyenne DDA Plan of Development’ presented
by the Downtown Development Authority of the City of Cheyenne. (Sponsors
— Mr.
Roybal and Mr. Segrave).
Mr. White moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Aldrich.
Motion carried with Dr. Aldrich and Mr.
White voting “YES” and Mr. Moody voting “NO.”
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Director, provided a staff report and memo outlining
questions and concerns from the public hearing held at the meeting of the governing body on
February 10, 2025.
Committee members Aldrich, Moody and White commented on the item.
Public comments were made by Brian Bau and Wendy yolk. Downtown Development Authority
Board members: Susan Allen; and Glen Garrett. Ward I Councilman, Pete Laybourn. also
commented on the item.
There being no further items for the agenda to come befbre the Public Services Committee, the
meeting was adjourned at 1:12 p.m.
```

